From: OpenLogi contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:26:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(desktop): state for editing stored G-series profiles

Reads a mouse's stored profiles through the agent, keeps one edit per
mouse, saves it with the sector bytes it started from, and selects a
profile. Each read and save carries a request number, so a late answer
can't overwrite newer state. A refused save keeps the edit; one refused
because the mouse changed meanwhile drops it, so the next edit starts
from a fresh read.

The mouse is the only store: nothing touches config.toml. The editor
screens come next.
